condition_name: The Empty Scrotum
condition_slug: the-empty-scrotum
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A clinical situation in which the testis is absent from the scrotum. May be bilateral or unilateral
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[5]: Absence of one or both testes from the scrotum,Pain from trauma to the testis,Infertility (in adulthood),Atrophic testis,Inguinal hernia may be present on the affected side
investigations[6]: "Urinary 17-ketosteroids, gonadotropins",Serum testosterone,Ultrasonography,Computed tomography,Laparoscopy,Magnetic Resonance Imaging
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[1]: "Hormone therapy: Human chorionic gonadotropin 1,500 units/week intramuscularly, for a total of 9 injections - Applicable only to special cases"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[4]: Torsion of the spermatic cord,Trauma to the testis,Malignancy,Infertility
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment[1]: "Surgical treatment: In those with undescended testes bring testis down and fix it in the scrotum"
prognosis: null